# The release component catalog.
#
# A release is a set of components, not four hardcoded images. This file is the
# one place that says which components exist, what they are called, which
# repository each is published to, and whether a release may omit it.
#
# Several places necessarily carry their own copy of this list: `docker-bake.hcl`
# is HCL, the deploy workflows must not check out a moving branch to learn what
# a release is allowed to contain, and `ai-agent-deploy` and
# `ai-agent-release-retention` run from /usr/local/sbin with no repository in
# sight. `infra/tests/artifact-contract.sh` compares every one of those copies
# against this file, so adding a component is a change here plus whatever that
# test then reports as out of date -- rather than a change here that silently
# leaves five other lists behind.
#
# Format: <name> <repository> <required>
#
# `required: false` says a deployment may proceed without the component. The
# administrative surface is the first one: it is published and attested with
# every release, so a host never builds it from source, but only the staging
# composition runs it -- production does not compose the service at all, and
# the forced-command grammar will not carry its digest to a production host.
# Optional is not the same as arbitrary: an optional component still has to be
# listed here to be accepted at all.
backend backend true
backend-migration backend-migration true
web web true
platform platform true
admin admin false
